  "synopsis": [
    {
      "langue": "en",
      "text": "San Guo Zhi: Qun Xiong Zheng Ba (The Romance of Three Kingdoms: The Fight Of Heroes' Pleiades) is a fighting game in the setting of the Chinese era of Three Kingdoms made by ASDER at an unknown date. This, most likely, has nothing to do with Koei's Three Kingdoms-based 3D fighting game, Dynasty Warriors.\r\n\r\nThis game doesn't use a 'traditional' Street Fighter II engine, instead, it comes up with a heavily modified engine from Samurai Shodown. Several features that weren't present in any other fighting games on Famicom were included: a 'rage' gauge that may be refilled by holding BW+A and performing a super move when it's fully charged; three-tiered health bar; and, finally, the 'conquest' mode, where you have to eliminate all of your opponent's fortresses in order to win.\r\n\r\nThe game has six playable characters, with every of them selectable from the beginning (from left to right): Guan Yu, Zhang Fei, Huang Zhong, Cao Ren, Mei Ya [?] and Lu Bu. However, during the 'conquest' mode, there are two more characters that are not playable the regular way: Shi Ren and Xie Seng. Both of them are slightly overpowered but have only two tiers of health at the very beginning.\r\n\r\nIn the 'arcade' mode, the player should defeat all six opponents (including his clone) in a specified order. Only nine continues are available for this type of game.\r\n\r\n'Conquest' mode, in its' turn, proposes the player to choose one of two preset teams, with each having three characters. After the choice is done, the player has to decide which enemy's fortress he should siege. Once the fortress is selected, the attacker's staying on his own, while the defending side has Shi Ren, Xie Seng and the actual &quot;defender&quot; (stage &quot;owner&quot;) appearing in the same defined order, King of Fighters style. Should only the attacker defeat one of the opponents, his health's being fully restored. Once all three opponent's fortresses fall, the player wins."
    },
    {
      "langue": "fr",
      "text": "San Guo Zhi : Qun Xiong Zheng Ba (The Romance of Three Kingdoms : The Fight Of Heroes' Pleiades) est un jeu de combat dans le cadre de l'ère chinoise des Trois Royaumes réalisé par ASDER à une date inconnue. Il n'a vraisemblablement rien à voir avec Dynasty Warriors, le jeu de combat 3D de Koei basé sur les Trois Royaumes.\r\n\r\nCe jeu n'utilise pas le moteur &quot;traditionnel&quot; de Street Fighter II, mais plutôt un moteur fortement modifié de Samurai Shodown. Plusieurs caractéristiques qui n'étaient pas présentes dans les autres jeux de combat sur Famicom ont été incluses : une jauge de &quot;rage&quot; qui peut être remplie en maintenant BW+A et en effectuant un super mouvement lorsqu'elle est complètement chargée ; une barre de santé à trois niveaux ; et, enfin, le mode &quot;conquête&quot;, où vous devez éliminer toutes les forteresses de votre adversaire pour gagner."
    },
    {
      "langue": "de",
      "text": "San Guo Zhi: Qun Xiong Zheng Ba (Die Romanze der drei Königreiche: Der Kampf der Plejaden der Helden) ist ein Kampfspiel in der chinesischen Ära der drei Königreiche, das ASDER zu einem unbekannten Zeitpunkt gedreht hat. Dies hat höchstwahrscheinlich nichts mit Koeis 3D-Kampfspiel Dynasty Warriors zu tun, das auf Three Kingdoms basiert.\r\n\r\nDieses Spiel verwendet keine &quot;traditionelle&quot; Street Fighter II-Engine, sondern eine stark modifizierte Engine von Samurai Shodown. Einige Funktionen, die in keinem anderen Kampfspiel auf Famicom vorhanden waren, waren enthalten: eine Wutanzeige, die durch Halten von BW + A und Ausführen eines Superzuges nachgefüllt werden kann, wenn sie voll aufgeladen ist; dreistufige Gesundheitsleiste; und schließlich den Eroberungsmodus, in dem Sie alle Festungen Ihres Gegners beseitigen müssen, um zu gewinnen.\r\n\r\n"
    },
    {
      "langue": "es",
      "text": "San Guo Zhi: Qun Xiong Zheng Ba es un juego de lucha ambientado en la era de los Tres Reinos de China. Enfrenta a legendarios guerreros como Guan Yu, Zhang Fei y Lu Bu en intensos combates por la supremacía.\r\n\r\nCada luchador posee habilidades únicas y puede cargar su &quot;rabia&quot; para ejecutar devastadores movimientos especiales. Las batallas cuentan con una barra de salud de tres niveles, permitiendo combates estratégicos y prolongados.\r\n\r\nEl modo 'conquista' añade un desafío adicional: los jugadores deben eliminar las fortalezas enemigas para reclamar la victoria. En este modo, aparecen guerreros adicionales con más poder, pero con menor resistencia. Con cada enfrentamiento, la lucha por el dominio de los Tres Reinos se vuelve más intensa, poniendo a prueba la destreza, reflejos y estrategia de cada guerrero en este épico conflicto."
    },
    {
      "langue": "it",
      "text": "San Guo Zhi: Qun Xiong Zheng Ba (The Romance of Three Kingdoms: The Fight Of Heroes' Pleiades) è un gioco di combattimento ambientato nell'era cinese dei Three Kingdoms realizzato da ASDER in una data sconosciuta. Questo, molto probabilmente, non ha nulla a che fare con il gioco di combattimento 3D basato sui Tre Regni di Koei, Dynasty Warriors.\r\nnnQuesto gioco non utilizza un motore &quot;tradizionale&quot; di Street Fighter II, ma si presenta con un motore pesantemente modificato da Samurai Shodown. Sono state incluse diverse funzionalità che non erano presenti in nessun altro gioco di combattimento su Famicom: un indicatore &quot;rabbia&quot; che può essere ricaricato tenendo premuto BW+A ed eseguendo una super mossa quando è completamente carico; barra della salute a tre livelli; e, infine, la modalità &quot;conquista&quot;, in cui devi eliminare tutte le fortezze del tuo avversario per vincere."
    },
    {
      "langue": "pt",
      "text": "San Guo Zhi: Qun Xiong Zheng Ba (O Romance dos Três Reinos: A Luta das Plêiades dos Heróis) é um jogo de luta no cenário da era chinesa dos Três Reinos feito por ASDER em uma data desconhecida. Isso, provavelmente, não tem nada a ver com o jogo de luta 3D baseado em Três Reinos da Koei, Dynasty Warriors.\r\n\r\nEste jogo não usa um motor 'tradicional' de Street Fighter II, em vez disso, ele vem com um motor fortemente modificado de Samurai Shodown. Vários recursos que não estavam presentes em nenhum outro jogo de luta no Famicom foram incluídos: um medidor de 'raiva' que pode ser recarregado segurando BW + A e realizando um super movimento quando estiver totalmente carregado; barra de saúde de três camadas; e, finalmente, o modo 'conquista', onde você deve eliminar todas as fortalezas do seu oponente para vencer.\r\n\r\n"
    }
  ],
